## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP design with an extra edit dimension on a classic string problem; requires careful transitions for matches, edits, and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP on substrings (i, j)
- Extra dimension for edits (t)
- Transitions for match/mismatch with edits
- Path reconstruction and complexity trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxLPSWithEdits(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(0)));
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) for (let t=0;t<=k;t++) dp[i][i][t] = 1;
  for (let len=2; len<=n; len++) {
    for (let i=0; i+len-1<n; i++) {
      const j = i+len-1;
      for (let t=0; t<=k; t++) {
        let best = Math.max(dp[i+1][j][t], dp[i][j-1][t]);
        if (s[i] === s[j]) best = Math.max(best, dp[i+1][j-1][t] + 2);
        if (t >= 1) best = Math.max(best, dp[i+1][j-1][t-1] + 2);
        if (t >= 2) best = Math.max(best, dp[i+1][j-1][t-2] + 2);
        dp[i][j][t] = best;
      }
    }
  }
  return dp[0][n-1][k];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to require exactly k edits instead of at most?
- How to reduce space to O(n*k)?
- How to reconstruct the edited string and the subsequence?

## Why This Is Asked
New angle: per-block setup cost while selecting up to k blocks, non-overlapping; tests ability to derive a compact DP with prefix sums and a best-so-far trick; includes reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping subarrays with a per-block cost
- Prefix sums to compute block values quickly
- Best-so-far technique to achieve O(nk) time
- Reconstruction pointers for endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKBlocksWithCost(A, k, cost) {
  const n = A.length;
  const P = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) P[i] = P[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => new Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  const bestVal = new Array(k+1).fill(NEG);
  bestVal[0] = 0; // dp[0][0] - P[0]

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      const candidate = P[i] - cost + bestVal[t-1];
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i-1][t], candidate);
    }
    // update bestVal for next i
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      const val = dp[i][t-1] - P[i];
      if (val > bestVal[t]) bestVal[t] = val;
    }
  }
  return { dp, P };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests minimax-style DP with reconstruction for a classic game.

## Key Concepts
- Two-player DP with difference state
- Subarray DP and reconstruction path
- Time: O(n^2) space: O(n^2)

## Code Example
```javascript
// dp[i][j] denotes max diff for i..j
function maxFirstPlayer(values){
  const n = values.length; const dp = Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(n).fill(0));
  let total = values.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[i][i]=values[i];
  for(let len=2; len<=n; len++){
    for(let i=0;i+len-1<n;i++){
      const j=i+len-1;
      dp[i][j] = Math.max(values[i]-dp[i+1][j], values[j]-dp[i][j-1]);
    }
  }
  return (total + dp[0][n-1])/2;
}
```

